            <ArticleTitle>Baastrup's Disease: A Comprehensive Review of the Extant Literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331-334</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1878-8750(17)30155-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.wneu.2017.02.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reports of Baastrup disease have been underrepresented in the medical literature. Therefore, the current comprehensive review was performed by searching standard search engines using the terms &quot;Baastrup's,&quot; &quot;disease,&quot; &quot;lumbar,&quot; &quot;interspinous bursitis,&quot; and &quot;kissing spine disease.&quot; Baastrup disease appears to be more common than once believed. Baastrup disease is associated with other degenerative disease processes of the spine that could potentially lead a physician to perform unnecessary surgery. Appreciation of this disease and identification on imaging can improve diagnosis and appropriate treatment of associated back pain.</AbstractText>
